docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T16.md:12:The spec requires append-only event storage with compaction: at configurable intervals, write a full-state snapshot of graph and memory to a separate file, then truncate the event log to events after the snapshot timestamp. This task implements that snapshot writer, the bootstrap-from-snapshot loader that lets the daemon start without replaying full history, the daemon-managed background scheduler that runs compaction off the hot path, and the architecture doc that records the format version, schedule semantics, and recovery procedure. Snapshots are the only mechanism preventing unbounded event-log growth for long-running repos; without this task, the event log substrate is incomplete.
