docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T13.md:1:# T13 — Phase 2 — Event writer API + payload hashing + workspace scoping
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T13.md:12:This task implements the public writer that workflow tools, the MCP layer, and the consolidation engine use to append events. It computes the canonical payload hash (deterministic over sorted-key JSON of the typed payload), decides inline vs. spilled payload location based on a configurable size ceiling, enforces workspace scoping at the API boundary (the writer cannot accept envelopes whose workspace_id disagrees with the open store), and meets the spec's hot-path budget of P99 ≤5ms write latency on `prepare_change` and `get_context_capsule` paths. Without the writer, no event ever reaches the store.
