docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md:12:This task implements the public memory store API: create, read, update, delete, and the state-machine transitions over `VerificationStatus` (`unverified → in_review → verified`, plus `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`). Writes are idempotent on a caller-provided idempotency key so retries do not double-insert. Every status transition emits the right event via the T13 writer (`MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`) and records an evidence row pointing at the triggering event. Without this task, the redesigned schema has no callable API and Phase 4 retrieval has nothing to read.
