docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T12.log:2149:This task creates the durable, append-only SQLite tables that back the event log: `events` for envelope rows and `event_payloads` for spilled payloads larger than the inline ceiling. It defines the migration runner that creates the schema on a fresh `.lattice/events.db`, and the indexes that make task, session, workspace, and branch scoped reads bounded. The spec requires the event log to be append-only and replayable; this task is where that invariant is encoded in the schema (no UPDATE/DELETE triggers, monotonic event_id PK). Without these tables, T13 (writer) and T14 (reader) have nowhere to land.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T12.log:2183:6. In `events/store.rs`, define low-level row APIs that T13 writer and T14 reader will sit on top of: `insert_envelope_row(...)`, `insert_or_get_payload(...)`, `query_events_by_task(...)`, `query_events_by_session(...)`, `query_events_by_workspace_branch(...)`. Every SQL string uses `rusqlite::params!`; no `format!` of SQL.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/logs/T12.log:2217:- [ ] No deferred work: append-only triggers, indexes, spillover table, and migration runner all in this task; the writer (T13), reader (T14), and snapshot (T16) are sibling tasks.
