ract gate for Identity ↔ Event ↔ Memory.\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 16 files, then report file count + first 3 paths confirmed via ls. Do NOT modify tasks.json, context.md, or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code.","agentId":"ac92f5b374c3f7cf9","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 16 brief files written successfully.\n\n**File count: 16**\n\n**First 3 paths confirmed via ls:**\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R18.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R25.md`\n- `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R26.md`\n\n(Full set: T11–T17, R18, T19–T24, R25, R26.)\n\n**What was done:**\n- Read the spec (Phases 2/3, Storage Design, Memory Graph sections), the build context, the relevant tasks.json entries (lines 190–492 covering T11–R26), and the Cadres coding standard.\n- Wrote 14 task briefs and 2 review briefs at the requested paths, each following the exact template structures provided.\n- Each task file cites the matching spec heading via the anchor pattern, quotes 2–3 spec excerpts directly, lists files_expected and verification_commands verbatim from tasks.json, and gives 8–11 concrete steps tuned to the task type:\n  - T11: all 20 event kinds + envelope fields verbatim from spec §Event Log.\n  - T12: explicit column list for `events` and `event_payloads` with append-only triggers and indexes (task/session/workspace+branch/kind).\n  - T13: writer with payload hashing, spillover, workspace scoping, batched/sync flush; P99 budget called out (test sits in T17).\n  - T14: typed query builder with mandatory scope, ceilings, streaming, payload-corruption detection.\n  - T15: enumerates the workflow tools instrumented (`prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_conte